# Order matters: Pages applies the first matching rule; existing static files are served as is.
# WHY targets end in "/" instead of "index.html": Cloudflare rejects rewrites whose target would
# be normalized (strip ".html"/"/index") back into the same rule as an infinite loop (error
# 10021, workers-sdk#10992); "/v/" and "/" are already canonical and serve v/index.html and index.html.
# W-01 (TRD §9): every /v/<token> gets the static page in v/index.html, never the React app.
/v/* /v/ 200
# SP-2: no rule may touch /.well-known/* (Apple does not follow redirects); the files win once they exist.
/* / 200
